WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:59.000
A splash of fresh water will reach the depths of your heart. Those mighty blue waves can propel you forward or they can calm and soothe. Coast to Michigan coast. Simply feel the flow in the moment. And let those vast lakes, rivers and streams create everlasting memories. Jump right in and let fresh wash over you in Pure Michigan. Keep it fresh at Michigan.org. Or on our website.
清凉的泉水会触动你的心弦。那汹涌的蓝色波浪既能推动你前行，也能让你平静舒缓。从密歇根的海岸到海岸。只需感受当下的流动。让那些广阔的湖泊、河流和溪流创造永恒的记忆。纵身跃入，让纯净的密歇根洗涤你的身心。在 Michigan.org 保持清新。或访问我们的网站。

2
00:00:59.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Due to the nature of this crime, case file has elected to change the names of some individuals featured in this episode. In 1992, newlyweds John and Lisa Schneeberger were living a charmed life together in the small farming community of Kipling, Saskatchewan. John was one of just two doctors in Kipling and every time Lisa went into town, she was stopped in the street by well-meaning locals who told her how lucky she was to be married to such a wonderful man. She entirely agreed with them. Their relationship hadn't exactly begun in a conventional way. In the fall of 1987, Lisa had been working as a receptionist at a medical clinic in Oxbow, another small town situated roughly 116 kilometers south of Kipling. She met John when he arrived at the clinic to work as a physician. The 26-year-old doctor had only recently relocated to Canada from South Africa as he'd wanted to escape the political turmoil of his homeland.
由于本案的性质，Case File 决定更改本集节目中部分相关人员的姓名。1992 年，新婚夫妇约翰和丽莎·施尼伯格在萨斯喀彻温省基普林的一个小型农业社区过着令人羡慕的生活。约翰是基普林仅有的两名医生之一，每当丽莎进城时，总会有好心的当地人拦住她，告诉她能嫁给这样一位出色的男人是多么幸运。她完全同意他们的看法。他们的关系开始得并不算传统。1987 年秋，丽莎在奥克斯博的一家医疗诊所担任接待员，那是位于基普林以南约 116 公里处的另一个小镇。她是在约翰来到诊所担任医生时认识他的。这位 26 岁的医生刚从南非移居加拿大，因为他想逃离祖国的政治动荡。

3
00:02:12.000 --> 00:03:18.000
John Schneeberger quickly became a popular figure at the small clinic, with patients finding him warm and personable. But he was still new to the country and didn't have many friends, so Lisa made an effort to be kind. She and her then-husband Rich began inviting John to have dinner with them, and gradually, something shifted in Lisa and John's dynamic. They grew closer, and Lisa's relationship with Rich, who had been her high school sweetheart, began to suffer. By the spring of 1988, Lisa and Rich had split up, and Lisa embarked on a romance with John. She took her young son and daughter to move to Kipling, and John went to, taking on a role as a doctor at the town's only hospital. Despite these sudden and drastic changes, the newly formed family adapted well. John was a loving stepfather to Lisa's two children, and they, in turn, adored him.
约翰·施尼伯格很快成为这家小诊所里的红人，病人们觉得他热情且平易近人。但他对这个国家来说还是个新人，没什么朋友，所以丽莎努力对他表示友好。她和当时的丈夫里奇开始邀请约翰共进晚餐，渐渐地，丽莎和约翰之间的互动发生了一些微妙的变化。他们变得亲近起来，而丽莎与高中恋人里奇的关系开始恶化。到 1988 年春天，丽莎和里奇分道扬镳，丽莎与约翰坠入爱河。她带着年幼的儿子和女儿搬到了基普林，约翰也随之而去，在镇上唯一的医院担任医生。尽管发生了这些突然而剧烈的变化，这个新组建的家庭适应得很好。约翰是丽莎两个孩子慈爱的继父，而孩子们也同样爱戴他。

4
00:03:18.000 --> 00:04:38.000
The townsfolk of Kipling were as charmed by John as those in Oxbow had been, and affectionately referred to him as Dr. John. Lisa and John designed and built their dream home, a spacious lakeside property with enough room for more children down the track. In 1991, they married. As far as Lisa was concerned, she had found her soulmate, and couldn't wait to spend the rest of her life with him. Music On Sunday, November 1, 1992, there was a knock at the Schneeberger's front door. Lisa went to answer it, and, to her surprise, saw an officer from the Royal Canadian Mounted Police standing on the stoop. Identifying himself as Detective Hansstra, he asked if he could speak to her husband.
基普林的镇民和奥克斯博的人们一样被约翰所吸引，亲切地称他为“约翰医生”。丽莎和约翰设计并建造了他们的梦想家园，那是一处宽敞的湖畔房产，有足够的空间容纳未来更多的孩子。1991 年，他们结婚了。在丽莎看来，她找到了灵魂伴侣，迫不及待地想与他共度余生。音乐 1992 年 11 月 1 日，星期日，施尼伯格家的前门响起了敲门声。丽莎去开门，惊讶地看到一位加拿大皇家骑警站在门廊上。他自称是汉斯特拉警探，询问是否可以和她的丈夫谈谈。

5
00:04:38.000 --> 00:05:47.000
Lisa called for John, and the two men stepped into another room to speak privately. Detective Hansstra informed John that he was investigating a very serious allegation. A patient had accused John of sexual assault. 23-year-old Candace Foster had filed a report earlier that morning, alleging that Dr. Schneeberger had drugged and raped her the previous night, when she attended the hospital where he worked for treatment. Detective Hansstra had already paid a visit to Kipling Memorial Union Hospital and interviewed the nurses on duty. One confirmed that Candace had arrived in a highly agitated state after getting into an argument with her boyfriend that had turned physical. A nurse had asked Candace if she would like to see Dr. Schneeberger, and she agreed. The doctor gave Candace a sedative that was used to treat severe agitation, and she stayed at the hospital overnight for monitoring.
丽莎叫来了约翰，两人走进另一个房间私下交谈。汉斯特拉警探告知约翰，他正在调查一起非常严重的指控。一名病人指控约翰性侵。23 岁的坎迪斯·福斯特当天早上早些时候提交了一份报告，声称施尼伯格医生在前一天晚上她去他工作的医院接受治疗时，给她下了药并强奸了她。汉斯特拉警探已经走访了基普林纪念联合医院，并采访了当值的护士。其中一名护士证实，坎迪斯在与男友发生肢体冲突后，情绪非常激动地来到医院。护士问坎迪斯是否想见施尼伯格医生，她同意了。医生给坎迪斯注射了一种用于治疗严重躁动的镇静剂，她留在医院过夜接受观察。

6
00:05:47.000 --> 00:06:53.000
Neither of the two nurses on duty had seen anything suspicious, and both had been frequently bustling in and out of the examination room where Candace was treated. The only other male in the entire hospital that night was a man whose wife was giving birth, and he had been in the delivery suite the entire time. John Schneeberger listened as the detective relayed the accusation against him. When it came time for him to speak, he adamantly denied the allegations, stating, It wasn't me. I would never have done that. John explained that when Candace had arrived, she was hysterical and said she felt like killing her boyfriend. He had asked if she would like something to calm down, and Candace said yes, so he'd given her a sedative called Versed. John theorized that perhaps the drug had caused Candace to hallucinate and mistakenly imagine an assault.
两名当值护士都没有发现任何可疑之处，而且她们经常进出坎迪斯接受治疗的检查室。那天晚上整个医院里唯一的另一名男性是一位妻子正在分娩的男子，他一直待在产房里。约翰·施尼伯格听着警探转述对他的指控。轮到他说话时，他坚决否认了这些指控，并说：“那不是我。我绝不会做那种事。”约翰解释说，坎迪斯到达时歇斯底里，说她想杀了她的男友。他问她是否需要镇静一下，坎迪斯说好，所以他给她注射了一种叫“咪达唑仑”的镇静剂。约翰推测，也许是药物导致坎迪斯产生了幻觉，从而错误地想象出了一场袭击。

7
00:06:53.000 --> 00:07:59.000
His description of the night's events were consistent with the nurses' accounts. Traces of Versed had also been found in Candace's system, so it was evident that the doctor was telling the truth about that as well. There was one easy way to get to the bottom of the matter. When Candace had gone to the police, she had brought a pair of underpants with her that she said she'd been wearing the night before. There was a semen stain on them that she insisted belonged to Dr Schneeberger. Investigators intended to obtain a DNA profile from the stain, and Detective Hansstra asked the doctor if he would be willing to provide a blood sample to compare with the result. Eager to clear his name, Dr Schneeberger said that he would be more than happy to oblige. The doctor soon made an appointment with the local police to give blood.
他对当晚事件的描述与护士们的陈述一致。坎迪斯的体内也发现了咪达唑仑的痕迹，因此很明显，医生在这一点上也说了实话。要查明真相有一个简单的方法。坎迪斯去警察局时，带了一条她声称是前一天晚上穿的内裤。上面有一块精液污渍，她坚称那是施尼伯格医生的。调查人员打算从污渍中提取 DNA 图谱，汉斯特拉警探询问医生是否愿意提供血样进行比对。为了洗清自己的名声，施尼伯格医生表示他非常乐意配合。医生很快与当地警方预约了抽血时间。

8
00:07:59.000 --> 00:09:11.000
Candace Foster had reported the alleged rape to the Royal Canadian Mounted Police, or RCMP, in the Saskatchewan capital of Regina, about 150 kilometers from where she lived in Kipling. The Regina RCMP had subsequently handballed the case back to Kipling's detachment. A lab technician withdrew a small amount of blood from Dr Schneeberger's left arm, and then he was free to go. DNA was still in its infancy as a forensic tool, and it would take some time to receive the results. In the meantime, word got out around town that Dr Schneeberger had been accused of rape by Candace Foster. John Schneeberger was a highly popular figure, and many Kipling residents found the allegations impossible to believe. Not only did he have a reputation as a gentle and trustworthy doctor, but he had done so much for the town. John chaired a board for disabled adults. He had helped out two young men when they got into trouble with the law,
坎迪斯·福斯特向位于萨斯喀彻温省首府里贾纳的加拿大皇家骑警（RCMP）报告了这起所谓的强奸案，里贾纳距离她居住的基普林约 150 公里。里贾纳的皇家骑警随后将案件移交回了基普林分局。一名实验室技术员从施尼伯格医生的左臂抽取了少量血液，然后他就被允许离开了。DNA 作为一种法医工具尚处于起步阶段，获取结果需要一些时间。与此同时，镇上传出了施尼伯格医生被坎迪斯·福斯特指控强奸的消息。约翰·施尼伯格是一位非常受欢迎的人物，许多基普林居民觉得这些指控令人难以置信。他不仅以温和、值得信赖的医生形象著称，而且为小镇做了很多贡献。约翰曾担任残疾成人委员会的主席。当两名年轻人触犯法律时，他曾伸出援手，

9
00:09:11.000 --> 00:10:18.000
and he had helped Kipling build its very first outdoor swimming pool by leading its fundraising campaign. His accuser was less well-liked. Candace Foster was a young single mother who worked at a local gas station. People around Kipling saw her as a party girl with a quick temper. At a cabaret event that Dr Schneeberger had organised to raise money for the community pool, Candace had caused the scene by arguing with her boyfriend and punching him. As the rape accusation became the talk of the town, most people sided with the doctor. They suspected Candace was inventing a story because she had a crush on him, or maybe she was after his money. After all, if she had been attacked in an examination room, then why hadn't she said anything to the two nurses who were on duty that night? Finally, after several months of waiting, the DNA results came through.
他还通过领导筹款活动帮助基普林建造了第一个室外游泳池。他的指控者则没那么受欢迎。坎迪斯·福斯特是一位在当地加油站工作的年轻单身母亲。基普林周围的人认为她是一个脾气暴躁的“派对女孩”。在施尼伯格医生为社区游泳池筹款而组织的歌舞表演活动中，坎迪斯曾因与男友争吵并殴打他而闹事。随着强奸指控成为镇上的谈资，大多数人都站在医生这一边。他们怀疑坎迪斯是因为暗恋他而编造了故事，或者可能是为了他的钱。毕竟，如果她在检查室里遭到袭击，为什么她当时没有告诉当晚值班的两名护士呢？最终，在等待了几个月后，DNA 结果出来了。

10
00:10:18.000 --> 00:11:19.000
A profile had been created from the semen stain on Candace's underwear, and John Schneeberger was not a match. These results came as a relief to John and his wife Lisa. She had not believed the allegations for one moment, and finally there was proof that her husband was innocent. Now that DNA evidence had vindicated him, hopefully they could move on with their lives. Yet, to their shock and disbelief, Candace wasn't going away. John and Lisa found out through the police that Candace was still insisting she had been raped at the hospital and that Dr Schneeberger was responsible. She was demanding that they test his blood a second time. Dr Schneeberger duly agreed to provide the police with more blood for further testing.
根据坎迪斯内裤上的精液污渍制作的图谱显示，与约翰·施尼伯格不匹配。这些结果让约翰和他的妻子丽莎松了一口气。她一刻也没有相信过那些指控，现在终于有了证明她丈夫清白的证据。既然 DNA 证据已经为他平反，希望他们能继续生活。然而，令他们震惊和难以置信的是，坎迪斯并没有就此罢休。约翰和丽莎通过警方得知，坎迪斯仍然坚持说她在医院被强奸了，而且是施尼伯格医生所为。她要求对他的血液进行第二次检测。施尼伯格医生如约同意向警方提供更多血液进行进一步检测。

11
00:11:19.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Once again, his sample did not match the DNA from the semen stain on Candace's underwear. Dr Schneeberger was definitively ruled out as a suspect. Because DNA evidence was absolute, the police told Candace there was nothing else they could do, and in 1994, the case file was closed. Lisa couldn't understand what had prompted Candace to target her husband so persistently. She wondered if Candace was infatuated with John and determined to ruin their marriage, or maybe she was mentally unwell. Whatever the reason, Lisa was furious with her. She knew without a doubt that Candace wasn't the victim. John was.
他的样本再次与坎迪斯内裤上精液的 DNA 不匹配。施尼伯格医生被明确排除在嫌疑人之外。由于 DNA 证据是绝对的，警方告诉坎迪斯他们无能为力，1994 年，案件档案被关闭。丽莎无法理解是什么促使坎迪斯如此执着地针对她的丈夫。她怀疑坎迪斯是否迷恋约翰并决心破坏他们的婚姻，或者她是否精神不正常。无论原因是什么，丽莎都对她感到愤怒。她毫无疑问地知道，坎迪斯不是受害者。约翰才是。

12
00:12:16.000 --> 00:13:20.000
Life went on as normal, with Dr Schneeberger retaining his good standing in the community. Luckily, most people in the town believed in him wholeheartedly. Candace Foster made the decision to move 150km away to Regina, so the Schneebergers no longer had to worry about bumping into her down the street. Over the next couple of years, the rape claim faded into the past, and they moved on into their future together. The happy couple had two children, with their first daughter born in 1995 and their second in 1996. Life was good, and their family was finally complete. But still, the Schneebergers suspected that Candace was lurking about on the fringes of their lives. One day in 1996, a man approached John at work with an entry form for a raffle.
生活恢复了正常，施尼伯格医生在社区中保持着良好的声誉。幸运的是，镇上大多数人都全心全意地相信他。坎迪斯·福斯特决定搬到 150 公里外的里贾纳，这样施尼伯格夫妇就不必担心在街上偶遇她了。在接下来的几年里，强奸指控逐渐淡出人们的记忆，他们继续着未来的生活。这对幸福的夫妇有了两个孩子，第一个女儿出生于 1995 年，第二个出生于 1996 年。生活很美好，他们的家庭终于圆满了。但施尼伯格夫妇仍然怀疑坎迪斯潜伏在他们生活的边缘。1996 年的一天，一名男子在工作中找到约翰，递给他一张抽奖入场券。

13
00:13:20.000 --> 00:14:17.000
He explained that it was part of a radio station contest to win a diamond ring, and asked John if he would like to enter. John agreed. He filled out the form, then placed it into the accompanying envelope, licking its adhesive strip before sealing it. The stranger had watched him carefully the entire time. This incident took on a sinister new light when the Schneebergers cleaner approached them with some information. She knew Candace Foster's parents and had heard that Candace had hired a private investigator to keep digging into John. Lisa was angry that Candace still seemed hell-bent on destroying their lives. From then on, John sealed envelopes by using water from the kitchen tap, telling Lisa,
他解释说这是电台竞赛的一部分，奖品是一枚钻戒，并问约翰是否想参加。约翰同意了。他填好表格，然后将其放入随附的信封中，舔了舔粘胶条将其封好。那个陌生人全程都在仔细观察他。当施尼伯格家的清洁工带来一些消息时，这件事呈现出一种阴险的新色彩。她认识坎迪斯·福斯特的父母，并听说坎迪斯雇了一名私家侦探继续挖掘约翰的底细。丽莎很生气，坎迪斯似乎仍然一心想摧毁他们的生活。从那时起，约翰用厨房水龙头的水来封信封，并告诉丽莎：

14
00:14:17.000 --> 00:15:14.000
You can just never be too careful when people are accusing you of things you didn't do. On the afternoon of Friday, April 25, 1997, Lisa Schneeberger was at home when one of her daughters approached with a surprising question. 15-year-old Amy was Lisa's eldest child from her first marriage, and she wanted to know whether she could go and visit her biological father. The request caught Lisa off guard, as the family had already made weekend plans, and Amy was supposed to be babysitting. Lisa noticed that Amy's complexion was pale and her expression troubled. She asked her daughter what was wrong. In a halting voice, Amy replied, Mum, I have something to tell you.
“当人们指控你没做过的事情时，你永远怎么小心都不为过。”1997 年 4 月 25 日，星期五下午，丽莎·施尼伯格正在家中，这时她的一位女儿带着一个令人惊讶的问题走过来。15 岁的艾米是丽莎第一次婚姻中的长女，她想知道自己是否可以去探望她的亲生父亲。这个请求让丽莎措手不及，因为家里已经安排了周末计划，而且艾米本该负责照看孩子。丽莎注意到艾米的脸色苍白，表情困扰。她问女儿怎么了。艾米声音颤抖地回答：“妈妈，我有件事要告诉你。”

15
00:15:14.000 --> 00:16:03.000
She gestured for her mother to come with her and led Lisa to her bedroom. Amy walked over to her bed and pulled back the covers. Then she pointed at the mattress. Lisa looked at the spot her daughter was indicating. Lying there was an empty condom wrapper. Then Amy spoke. Mum, he's done this to me before. The night of October 31, 1992, wasn't shaping up to be a fun Halloween for 23-year-old Candace Foster. For starters, she had a shift at the gas station where she worked full-time.
她示意母亲跟她走，把丽莎带到了她的卧室。艾米走到床边，掀开被子。然后她指着床垫。丽莎看向女儿指的地方。那里躺着一个空的避孕套包装纸。接着艾米开口了：“妈妈，他以前也对我做过这种事。”1992 年 10 月 31 日的万圣节之夜，对于 23 岁的坎迪斯·福斯特来说，并不是一个愉快的夜晚。首先，她在全职工作的加油站有一个轮班。

16
00:16:03.000 --> 00:17:14.000
Candace had given birth to a baby girl nine months earlier, and as a single mother, she was solely responsible for providing for her daughter. Her parents, who came from a modest farming background, were supportive, but juggling parenthood with long working hours was exhausting. Second of all, Candace's boyfriend, Danny, had showed up at the gas station, which had led to an argument. Candace and Danny had a tumultuous relationship, and she'd just learned that he had lied to her about seeing other women. They began to fight, with Candace growing as distressed about the argument itself as she was about the fact it was taking place at her work. Danny made one last offensive retort, then jumped into his truck and drove away laughing with a friend. Furious, Candace kicked the side of the vehicle as it peeled out of the parking lot. She was so distraught and angry that she decided to go to Kipling Memorial Union Hospital to see a friend who worked there.
坎迪斯九个月前生下了一个女婴，作为单身母亲，她独自承担着抚养女儿的责任。她的父母来自普通的农家，虽然给予了支持，但兼顾育儿和长时间的工作让人精疲力竭。其次，坎迪斯的男友丹尼出现在加油站，导致了一场争吵。坎迪斯和丹尼的关系动荡不安，她刚刚得知他对自己撒谎，说他和其他女人见面。他们开始争吵，坎迪斯对争吵本身感到痛苦，就像她对这件事发生在工作场所感到痛苦一样。丹尼说了最后一句冒犯的话，然后跳上他的卡车，笑着和朋友开车离开了。愤怒的坎迪斯在车子驶出停车场时踢了车身一脚。她心烦意乱，愤怒不已，决定去基普林纪念联合医院看望一位在那里工作的朋友。

