艾米一直睡不着，所以继父给她注射了什么东西。第二天当她整理床铺时，她惊恐万分，发现床单间夹着一个避孕套包装纸。现在她有了长期以来一直发生的袭击的物证，艾米决定向母亲吐露心声。丽莎感到恶心，但她一秒钟也没有怀疑过女儿。记忆涌上心头，丈夫在孩子们不舒服时经常给他们注射，而不是提供药片或糖浆。丽莎问约翰为什么要这样做，他只是向她保证注射更快且非常有效。因为他是医生，她对他的回答很满意。丽莎记得有一次艾米醒来时感到恶心、昏昏沉沉且心烦意乱，哭着告诉母亲约翰在深夜给她打了一针。

37
00:34:47.000 --> 00:36:02.000
When Lisa asked him about it, he'd said, yes, she was coughing. Didn't you hear her coughing? Lisa hadn't heard any coughing, but she believed her husband. As she processed the fact that her life as she knew it was a lie and the enormity of Amy's suffering, Lisa asked her daughter why she hadn't come to her sooner. Amy replied, you didn't believe Candice, why would you believe me? In an instant, Lisa knew that Candice Foster had been telling the truth all along. As reported by Crime magazine, she later told the Canadian television program W5, I felt sick, I still blame myself. Maybe if I had believed Candice, none of this would have happened to my daughter. Lisa helped Amy pack a bag so she could stay elsewhere for the weekend. Then she called her husband on his cell phone.
