00:37:04.000 --> 00:38:23.000
After lifting it off and opening it up, Lisa saw it was filled with doctor's gloves, syringes, condoms and vials of a drug called Versed. A benzodiazepine medication, Versed is a sedative sometimes used to decrease agitation and induce sleepiness. It is also used for anesthesia and can cause those injected with it to lose consciousness. Additionally, Versed has an amnesiac effect, preventing the formation of new memories. Lisa placed a phone call to Detective Hansstra at the RCMP and reported her husband for rape, telling the detective everything that Amy had told her. When Candice learned that Dr Schneeberger had been accused of raping his stepdaughter repeatedly over the past two years, she burst into tears. Ever since she had been raped by the doctor in 1992, she had been terrified that he would do the same thing to other women. To learn that he had repeatedly victimized an underage girl was her greatest nightmare realized.
